{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2193-06-08 00:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good evening. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I understand you came in because your INR was low and you had a fall yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2193-06-08 00:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I fell off my horse—landed hard on my back. My head snapped down but I didn’t lose consciousness. They did a CT at the outside ER and said no bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2193-06-08 00:23:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And your INR was 1.7 when you got here. Because you have a mechanical mitral valve, we need your INR to stay above 3.0 for safety. That’s why we’re admitting you—to bridge with heparin until the warfarin catches up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2193-06-08 00:24:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I’ve been on warfarin for years. Why did it drop this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2193-06-08 00:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not entirely sure yet. Sometimes changes in diet, fluid intake, or other meds can affect it. We’ll monitor closely and adjust your dose before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2193-06-08 00:27:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been eating less since the fall—my back and side really hurt. I’ve been taking tramadol and gabapentin like usual, but it’s not helping much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2193-06-08 00:28:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll reassess your pain and see what we can safely add. Given your kidney disease, some pain meds aren’t safe, but we’ll find a balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2193-06-08 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night show your INR is still low at 2.0. We’ve started IV heparin to protect your valve while we adjust the warfarin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2193-06-08 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the heparin going to make me bleed? I’m on anticoagulants already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2193-06-08 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring your blood work closely to avoid that. The heparin is temporary—just until your INR comes up safely with warfarin. We’ll check it daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2193-06-08 08:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. My back pain is still bothering me—can we try something stronger?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2193-06-08 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can try a small dose of oral dilaudid, but we have to be very careful. With your kidney function, it can build up and affect your breathing or alertness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2193-06-08 08:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see. I guess I’d rather be a little uncomfortable than risk something serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2193-06-08 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you a low dose of dilaudid earlier. The nurse mentioned you became very drowsy and your breathing slowed. We gave narcan to reverse it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2193-06-08 12:31:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t remember that… I just felt really out of it. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2193-06-08 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not uncommon in patients with kidney disease. The medication wasn’t clearing from your system, so it built up. We’ll avoid that med now and stick to safer options."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2193-06-08 12:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m glad you caught it. Can we add something else for pain? Maybe more acetaminophen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2193-06-08 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we can safely add acetaminophen. We’ll start 1000 mg every 8 hours. It’s safer for your kidneys and won’t affect your breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2193-06-09 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had another episode of drowsiness last night after another dose. We gave narcan again. A CT of your head was done to rule out any bleeding—good news, it’s normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2193-06-09 07:47:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another one? I didn’t realize… So it’s definitely the medication, not a brain injury?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2193-06-09 07:48:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the CT shows no bleeding or injury. Your confusion and drowsiness are most likely from the dilaudid not clearing. We’ve stopped it completely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2193-06-09 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m relieved. I was worried something was really wrong with my head."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2193-06-09 07:51:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We were too, given your anticoagulation. But now we know it’s a medication effect. We’ll keep you on acetaminophen, tramadol, and gabapentin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2193-06-09 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your kidney function is still impaired. You received dialysis yesterday, and we’ll continue your immunosuppressants and other ESRD meds as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2193-06-09 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My peritoneal catheter isn’t working well yet, is it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2193-06-09 14:23:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not fully, no. It’s new, so it may take time. For now, we’re using your tunneled HD catheter for dialysis. We’ll follow up with your transplant team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2193-06-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 3.2—finally in the target range. We’re stopping the heparin and continuing warfarin at 5 mg daily for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2193-06-10 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good! So I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2193-06-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Almost. We want to see one more INR to confirm it stays stable. And we need to make sure your pain is manageable at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2193-06-10 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m doing better with the new pain meds. Still sore, but I can move around with my walker."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2193-06-10 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest INR is 3.5—perfect. We’ll switch you to warfarin 2 mg daily to avoid it going too high, especially if your appetite stays low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2193-06-10 15:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why lower the dose if it’s finally in range?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2193-06-10 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because your intake has been poor, and when you eat less, warfarin can become stronger. Lowering the dose helps prevent it from going too high once you’re home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2193-06-10 15:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ll be more careful with my diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2193-06-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had two clear head CTs, your mental status is normal, and your pain is controlled. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2193-06-11 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Will I need help at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2193-06-11 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your recent fall and ongoing pain, we recommend a home health aide for a few days. We’ll help you apply for that service."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2193-06-11 09:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I don’t want to fall again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2193-06-12 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. Your labs are stable, you’re walking independently, and your INR is at 3.5. We’ll discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2193-06-12 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2193-06-12 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take warfarin 2 mg every night. Check your INR tomorrow and call the coagulation clinic with the result. Continue your pain meds as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2193-06-12 10:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if my pain gets worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2193-06-12 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Try the acetaminophen first. If it’s not enough, call your PCP. We’ll also suggest a pain management consult if it continues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2193-06-12 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I’ll follow up with my transplant team about the PD catheter too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Your discharge instructions are ready, and the home health aide will contact you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I feel much better and safer now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: warfarin 2 mg tonight, INR test tomorrow, and call the coagulation clinic. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And no more horseback riding for a while!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Smart plan. Let’s get you healed first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad you’re doing well. Take it easy, and don’t hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:13:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your discharge papers and meds shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep an eye on the abrasion on your leg. Keep it clean and dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been doing that. It’s not infected, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of infection. Just keep it covered and monitor for redness or swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright, I’ll see you in follow-up if needed. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:25:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:28:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will assist you with discharge soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2193-06-13 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care and get some rest."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2193-06-08 00:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2193-06-13 21:43:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 60-year-old woman with end-stage renal disease, a mechanical mitral valve, and a history of multiple transplants was admitted for a subtherapeutic INR of 1.7 following a fall from a horse. She was started on heparin bridging and warfarin to achieve a target INR of 3.0–3.5. During her stay, she experienced poorly controlled back pain, which led to two episodes of somnolence and respiratory depression after oral dilaudid administration, both reversed with narcan. Head CT scans showed no acute intracranial abnormalities, confirming the altered mental status was due to opioid toxicity. Her INR stabilized at 3.5, and she was discharged on warfarin 2 mg daily with instructions to follow up with the coagulation clinic. Pain management was optimized with acetaminophen, tramadol, and gabapentin, and a home health aide was arranged for support. She remained hemodynamically stable, mentated appropriately, and ambulatory with a walker at discharge.",
    "problems": [
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Head injury, unspecified",
      "Backache, unspecified",
      "Generalized pain",
      "Accident involving animal being ridden injuring rider of animal",
      "Altered mental status",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Complications of transplanted organ, unspecified",
      "Chronic systolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Peripheral vascular disease, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Awaiting organ transplant status"
    ]
  }
}
